It *doesn't* always returns that. The higher your dexterity, the smaller
the chance you'll fail.

Also, you can (s)earch a chest to find possible traps, before you kick or
try to untrap them.

If after, say, ten searches, you haven't found a trap yet, chances are
that they're not trapped at all, and you can try to open them.

Kicking chests is, in general, a bad idea. You'll destroy potions, glass
objects, crystal objects, and possible some more things I forgot.

